                           S I C K     C H A T 
          - - ----------------------------------------------- - -

                           By Zed Of CDTE-SoFT

			  FOR DAYDREAM BBS 1.20+


Purpose:
~~~~~~~~
	Replace DayDream's internal split screen chatter with a more
featureful one.

Features:
~~~~~~~~~
- Split Screen
- Partial Screen Scroll
- Real time moving clock at bottom
- Chat timer at bottom
- CTRL-Z gives you a temporary line chat
- Macros
- Different colors for different character types
  (letters, numbers, etc)
- CTRL-L only clears your chat window and not the user's.
- SysOp can swap windows with user by pressing CTRL-S
- CTRL-R redraws the screen
- User can upload straight into chat, files saved into SysOp's
  upload dir as defined in DayDream's Main Config.



Installation:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
	Put "Doors:Sick-Chat %N" into the MUIConfig proggy. This should
be in the ChatDoor text box. Make sure you change the cycle-gadget to DOOR
also. Now just hit AMIGA - and it will load Sick Chat.

If you don't use the MUIConfig prog, then edit your config like this:

CHATMODE..... D
CHATCMD...... doors:sick-chat %N



Macros:
~~~~~~~
	An example macro file is included. Sick-Chat.Macros goes into
DayDream:Configs/. The structure is as follows:

NUMBER OF MACROS
STRING TO DETECT
REPLACEMENT STRING

Example:

1
BBS
Bulletin Board

 With the above config, if a user types "BBS", "Bulletin Board" will appear
instead. No real practical use for this feature, but it looks good :)


